From 4792b8e79d0f376c674f24feb0d2fadde10829cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:30:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a done ordering prerequisite does not hold a
 reviewed PR owner

A PR owner parked with kanban_block(kind="dependency") on an exact-head
review AND an ordering prerequisite (a base-CI repair card whose result
carries no verdict) was held `active_pr` until its PR merged or closed.
Only the owner can merge it, so it deadlocked into the hold cap and a
supervisor escalation (hub t_9eca225b1a9f8451, PR #3295: approve at an
exact head plus a done base repair superseded by PR #3296).

Five whys:
1. Why held? active_pr_reason found no handoff after the PR comment.
2. Why no ordering handoff? _dependency_handoff_after refuses any awaited
   parent whose result is_review_result, deferring to the review rules.
3. Why no review continuation? resumes_review required every awaited
   parent to approve or leave repair evidence, the repair card included.
4. Why can the repair card not satisfy it? It reviews nothing; it has no
   verdict and no exact head.
5. Why did neither path cover it? Each assumed an all-review or
   all-ordering awaited set; a mixed set matched neither.

Fix: in resumes_review, a parent the checkpoint named as awaited that is
done and whose latest result is not a review result (local run, else the
foreign-parent mirror kanban_move_parent_results row with parent_status
done) is a completed ordering prerequisite: it neither authorizes nor
refuses. A historical parent reopened after the park, a late-linked
parent and every legacy-checkpoint parent keep the review rules. The
remaining review parents still meet the existing exact-head approval/repair rules
and must cover every holding PR. At least one review parent must remain;
an all-ordering park keeps the ordering handoff unchanged. One
continuation, crash/reclaim and foreign owner-fault refusals unchanged.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dependency_review_ordering_parent.py
- local mixed park resumes once (claim consumes, reclaim stays held) and
  the hub-shaped foreign variant (parents only in the mirror) dispatches
  on the importing worker: both RED on 208402a5bd, GREEN with the fix.
- negatives: ordering parent not done, approval without exact head, of an
  unrelated PR, or a lost-verdict review naming the PR all stay held;
  REQUEST_CHANGES at an exact head still hands back for repair;
  a legacy checkpoint (no awaited list) keeps the per-parent rule;
  all-ordering parks still resume only through the ordering handoff.
